0,Central Solomon languages - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Central_Solomon_languages,"The Central Solomon languages are the four Papuan languages spoken in the state of Solomon Islands. The four languages are, listed from northwest to southeast, Savosavo of Savo Island. The four Central Solomon languages were identified as a family by Wilhelm Schmidt in 1908.",Touo,Central Solomons
1,Touo language - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Touo_language,"The Touo language, also known as Baniata (Mbaniata) or Lokuru, is spoken over the southern part of Rendova Island, located in the Western Province of the Solomon Islands.",Touo,Central Solomons
