9,New Arguments for a Central Solomons Family Based on Evidence...,https://www.jstor.org/stable/43897708,"In the Solomon Islands, four Papuan languages are spoken: Savosavo, Touo, Lavukaleve, and Bilua.This syncretism, together with the very similar first and second person pronominal paradigms, are adduced as new arguments in favor of the existence of a Central Solomons family.",Touo,Central Solomons
